  "courseName": "Introductory Molecular Biology (200-level)",
  "estimatedLength": "35 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the three-dimensional components of DNA\u2014two antiparallel sugar-phosphate backbones and inward-projecting nitrogenous bases\u2014and describe how they assemble into a double helix.",
    "Apply complementary base-pair rules (A\u2013T with two hydrogen bonds; G\u2013C with three hydrogen bonds) to infer one strand from the other.",
    "Explain how antiparallel orientation and backbone directionality create 5'\u21923' synthesis constraints.",
    "Trace the replication fork sequence (helicase, SSBs, DNA polymerase, DNA ligase) and match each step to its function.",
    "Explain why leading synthesis is continuous while lagging synthesis is discontinuous (Okazaki fragments) based on polymerase 5'\u21923' directionality on antiparallel templates.",
    "Explain semiconservative replication and predict daughter-molecule composition after one and two rounds. "
  ],
